<title>USA: US fines RMI Titanium over trade violations.</title>
<headline>US fines RMI Titanium over trade violations.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Commerce Department said Wednesday it imposed a fine of $160,000 against RMI Titanium Co to settle allegations of illegal trade.</p>
<p>The company made six shipments of titanium alloy products to France and Israel without obtaining export licenses required under the Export Administration Act, the department said.</p>
<p>RMI agreed to pay the civil penalty, but did not admit or deny the allegations, the department said in a statement.</p>
</text>
